          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            is
            %strong exhaustive
            if it has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            of (transfinite) sequences of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
            which interact well with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p Given a transfinite sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0 \to A_1 \to \cdots
          %p
            (continuing through
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\alpha
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\lt\kappa
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            is some limit
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal"} ordinal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi α
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\alpha \to A_\beta
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\kappa
            is a colimit of this sequence (a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
            = succeed "." do
              %strong transfinite union
          %p
            A category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            %strong exhaustive
            if one, hence both, of the following two equivalent conditions hold.
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                has transfinite unions which are stable under pullback and for which the coprojections
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi α
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\alpha \to A_\kappa
                are also monomorphisms.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                has transfinite unions, and given any diagram
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi B
                                %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi B
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mi ⋯
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi B
                                %mi κ
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %mi ⋯
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi κ
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      B_0 &amp; \to &amp; B_1 &amp; \to &amp; \cdots &amp; \to &amp; B_\kappa\\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                      A_0 &amp; \to &amp; A_1 &amp; \to &amp; \cdots &amp; \to &amp; A_\kappa\\
                      }
              %p
                in which the bottom row is a transfinite union and for each
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi β
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\lt\beta\lt\kappa
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi B
                                %mi α
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi B
                                %mi β
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi α
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{ B_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; B_\beta \\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow \\
                      A_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; A_\beta }
              %p
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
                (hence
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi α
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi β
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_\alpha \to B_\beta
                is also monic), then the top row is a transfinite union (i.e. a colimit diagram) if and only if for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\lt\kappa
                the square
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi B
                                %mi α
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi B
                                %mi κ
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi α
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi A
                                %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{ B_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; B_\kappa \\
                      \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow \\
                      A_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; A_\kappa }
              %p
                is a pullback. (In other words, transfinite unions are
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/van+Kampen+colimits"} van Kampen colimits
          %p
            Note that half of the second condition is simply that the colimits in the first condition are stable under pullback. One may obtain various weaker notions by restricting the allowable values of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p
            We will prove the equivalence of these two characterizations in Propositions
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoprojectionsMonic"}
            and
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AlternativeCharacterization"}
            below.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                is easily verified to be exhaustive.
            %li
              %p
                Since limits and colimits in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} presheaf categories
                are pointwise, any presheaf category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi D
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D^{op},Set]
                is also exhaustive.
            %li
              %p
                Since the condition involves only colimits and finite limits, it is preserved by any
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} left exact localization
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
                is exhaustive.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p We first prove the equivalence of the above two definitions.
          #CoprojectionsMonic.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p In a category which satisfies the second definition above, given a transfinite union
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_0 \to A_1 \to \cdots \to A_\kappa
            %p
              (so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\alpha \to A_\beta
              is monic for all
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi β
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\lt\beta\lt\kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\alpha\to A_\kappa
              are also monic.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              For a fixed
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi α
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mrow
                                %mi α
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi κ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    A_0 &amp; \to &amp; A_1 &amp; \to &amp; \cdots &amp; \to &amp; A_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; A_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; \cdots &amp; \to &amp; A_\alpha\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                    A_0 &amp; \to &amp; A_1 &amp; \to &amp; \cdots &amp; \to &amp; A_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; A_{\alpha+1} &amp; \to &amp; \cdots &amp; \to &amp; A_\kappa\\
                    }
            %p It is easy to see that each intermediate square is a pullback, and of course the top row is a colimit. Thus, in particular the square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi α
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{ A_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; A_\alpha \\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                    A_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; A_\kappa}
            %p
              is a pullback, i.e.
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\alpha\to A_\kappa
              is monic.
          #AlternativeCharacterization.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              satisfies the first condition above, i.e. it has pullback-stable transfinite unions for which the coprojections are also monic. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              also satisfies the second condition above.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p It remains to show that given a diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi κ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 0
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi κ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi κ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    B_0 &amp; \to &amp; B_1 &amp; \to &amp; \cdots &amp; \to &amp; B_\kappa\\
                    \\downarrow^{f_0} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{f_1} &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{f_\kappa}\\
                    A_0 &amp; \to &amp; A_1 &amp; \to &amp; \cdots &amp; \to &amp; A_\kappa\\
                    }
            %p in which both rows are transfinite compositions of monomorphisms and the squares
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi β
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi α
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi β
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{ B_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; B_\beta \\
                    \\downarrow^{f_\alpha} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{f_\beta} \\
                    A_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; A_\beta }
            %p are pullbacks, also the squares
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi κ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi α
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi κ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi α
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{ B_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; B_\kappa \\
                    \\downarrow^{f_\alpha} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{f_\kappa} \\
                    A_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; A_\kappa }
            %p are pullbacks.
            %p
              Fix an
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\lt\kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon X\to B_\kappa
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi κ
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\kappa g
              factors through
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\alpha
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              factors through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_\alpha
              = succeed "-colimit" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              and the
              = succeed "-colimit" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi κ
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\kappa g
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi κ
                            %mi g
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi κ
                            %mi g
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋯
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    g^*B_0 &amp; \to &amp; g^*B_1 &amp; \to &amp; \cdots &amp; \to &amp; X\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp;&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{1_X}\\
                    (f_\kappa g)^* A_0 &amp; \to &amp; (f_\kappa g)^* A_1 &amp; \to &amp; \cdots &amp; \to &amp; X\\
                    }
            %p and it is easy to verify, by the pasting law for pullbacks, that each square
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi β
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi γ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi β
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mi γ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi κ
                            %mi g
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi β
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi κ
                            %mi g
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{ g^* B_\beta &amp; \to &amp; g^* B_\gamma \\
                    \\downarrow^{f_\beta} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{f_\gamma} \\
                    (f_\kappa g)^* A_\beta &amp; \to &amp; (f_\kappa g)^* A_\gamma }
            %p
              is a pullback for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi β
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi γ
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta\lt\gamma\lt\kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi κ
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\kappa g
              factors through
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi α
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\alpha
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi κ
                    %mi g
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi β
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi κ
                    %mi g
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_\kappa g)^* A_\beta \to (f_\kappa g)^* A_\gamma
              is split epic whenever
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi β
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha\lt\beta\lt\gamma
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi β
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^* B_\beta \to g^* B_\gamma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^* B_\alpha \to X
              is an isomorphism; hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              factors through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_\alpha
              as desired.
          %p
            Exhaustiveness also interacts well with other
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exactness+properties"} exactness properties
          #FinInfExtensive.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If an exhaustive category is also finitary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              A coproduct of cardinality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              can be constructed using transfinite compositions and finite coproducts:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi κ
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{\alpha\lt 0} A_\alpha \to \sum_{\alpha\lt 1} A_\alpha \to \sum_{\alpha\lt 2} A_\alpha \to \cdots \to \sum_{\alpha\lt \kappa} A_\alpha
            %p
              Finitary extensivity implies that all the transition maps are monic, so that these transfinite composites exist in an exhaustive category. Pullback-stability of coproducts follows easily from pullback-stability of transfinite unions and of finite coproducts. Finally, it is known (see
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
          %p Colimits in an exhaustive category preserve finite limits.
          #UnionsPreserveIntersections.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              In an exhaustive category, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_\alpha)_{\alpha\lt\kappa}
              and also a sequence
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B_\alpha)_{\alpha\lt\kappa}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_\alpha\cap B_\alpha)_{\alpha\lt\kappa}
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
              being taken as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Since transfinite unions are stable under pullback,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the colimit of the
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi κ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi κ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\kappa\times\kappa)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi α
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi β
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi κ
                          %mo ,
                          %mi β
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_\alpha\cap B_\beta)_{\alpha\lt\kappa, \beta\lt\kappa}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/final+functor"} final
          #UnionsPreservePullbacks.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              In an exhaustive category, given a pullback diagram of
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi A
                                  %mi α
                              %mtd
                                %mo →
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi B
                                  %mi α
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi C
                                  %mi α
                              %mtd
                                %mo →
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi D
                                  %mi α
                        %mo )
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(\array{ A_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; B_\alpha \\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                    C_\alpha &amp; \to &amp; D_\alpha }\right)_{\alpha\lt\kappa}
            %p the induced square of colimits:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi κ
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi κ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi κ
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{ A_\kappa &amp; \to &amp; B_\kappa \\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                    C_\kappa &amp; \to &amp; D_\kappa }
            %p is also a pullback.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_5 Proof
            %p
              Define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              so that the following square is a pullback:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi B
                              %mi κ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo
                              %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi κ
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi D
                              %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{ P &amp; \overset{f}{\to} &amp; B_\kappa \\
                    ^g\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                    C_\kappa &amp; \to &amp; D_\kappa }
            %p
              Since pullbacks preserve transfinite unions,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is the transfinite union of the sequnece
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^* B_\alpha)_{\alpha\lt\kappa}
              and also the sequence
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g^* C_\alpha)_{\alpha\lt\kappa}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UnionsPreserveIntersections"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is also the transfinite union of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mi α
                      %mo ∩
                      %msup
                        %mi g
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f^* B_\alpha\cap g^* C_\alpha)_{\alpha\lt\kappa}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi D
                      %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_\alpha \to D_\kappa
              are monic, it is straightforward to verify that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi α
                    %mo ∩
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi α
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi D
                          %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi α
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^* B_\alpha\cap g^* C_\alpha \cong B_\alpha \times_{D_\alpha} C_\alpha \cong A_\alpha.
            %p
              Thus,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is the transfinite union of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi α
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mi α
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_\alpha)_{\alpha\lt\kappa}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo ≅
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\cong A_\kappa
          #UnionsPreserveMonos.num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              In an exhaustive category, transfinite unions preserve monomorphisms. That is, given a transformation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi α
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi α
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_\alpha \to B_\alpha)_{\alpha\lt\kappa}
              of transfinite sequences of monomorphisms which is pointwise monic, also the induced map on colimits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi κ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_\kappa\to B_\kappa
              is monic.
